WEBVTT

00:00:03.506 --> 00:00:12.086
Loan Servicing
Looking after loans once they are booked: the loan book, PLR changes and early-warning collections.

00:00:12.102 --> 00:00:15.577
The loan book is a daily snapshot from the loan system (LMS)
The LMS stays the system of record — the CRM services from it

00:00:15.577 --> 00:00:24.821
Sign in as Rajiv Doorgakant — Manager, Loans & Fixed Income
Loans manager — reviews the book every morning

00:00:24.821 --> 00:00:28.558
Lending ▸ Loan Servicing ▸ Loan Book: one row per loan account
Rate, days in arrears, arrears bucket, maturity and LTV for every account

00:00:28.558 --> 00:00:37.498
Show only the accounts in arrears: search for “In arrears”
Sort by any column — e.g. days in arrears

00:00:37.498 --> 00:00:39.693
Open LMS-100202 — a home loan 45 days in arrears

00:00:39.693 --> 00:00:43.329
Outstanding principal and the current rate: PLR minus the product margin
Variable (PLR-linked) loans follow every PLR change

00:00:43.329 --> 00:00:49.455
Monthly instalment and the next due date
Borrowers get an SMS reminder three days before each instalment, in their language

00:00:49.455 --> 00:00:56.163
Days and amount in arrears, the bucket, maturity and the current LTV
An account entering arrears opens a collections follow-up for its RM automatically

00:00:56.163 --> 00:01:01.659
ALCO has decided to cut the Genesis PLR by 25 bps, from 6.825% to 6.575%
The loans executive drafts the campaign that tells every variable-rate borrower

00:01:01.659 --> 00:01:09.121
Sign in as Sophie Lagesse — Loans Executive
Loans executive — prepares the campaign

00:01:09.121 --> 00:01:11.975
Loan Servicing ▸ PLR Change ▸ New: old rate, new rate, effective date

00:01:11.975 --> 00:01:17.531
“Approved by” stays empty — the campaign is only a draft
A small, realistic change keeps the demo book sensible

00:01:17.531 --> 00:01:20.299
The campaign starts in Draft
Draft ▸ Approved ▸ Notices generated ▸ Distributed

00:01:20.299 --> 00:01:23.773
Try to move it to Approved…

00:01:23.773 --> 00:01:28.073
Blocked: an approval must name the approver (the ALCO decision)
The loans manager signs the campaign off — not the person who drafted it

00:01:28.073 --> 00:01:33.613
Meanwhile, the RM works the early-warning follow-ups
Each account in arrears got a call to make, opened by the daily arrears check

00:01:33.613 --> 00:01:42.012
Sign in as Bruno Chan — Relationship Manager (Corporate)
Relationship manager — owns the borrowers in arrears

00:01:42.012 --> 00:01:45.776
Loan Servicing ▸ Collections: arrears bucket, action, date and outcome
History stays on the list: earlier calls, demand letters, disputes

00:01:45.776 --> 00:01:56.175
Log the call on LMS-100202: the borrower promises to pay
Edit the follow-up the CRM opened and record the outcome

00:01:56.175 --> 00:01:57.347
Save without the promised date…

00:01:57.347 --> 00:02:01.303
Refused: a promise to pay needs the amount and the date
So nobody chases a promise without knowing when it is due

00:02:01.303 --> 00:02:06.209
Add the date she gave and save again

00:02:06.209 --> 00:02:13.324
The promise is written on the loan account
Promise to pay by: the date everyone sees on the loan

00:02:13.324 --> 00:02:28.966
LMS-08810: 95 days, no contact, and the demand letter is disputed
Time to escalate — log a new collections action

00:02:28.966 --> 00:02:32.007
Escalated — the loans manager is alerted at once
Bucket 90+: the case now follows the legal recovery route

00:02:32.007 --> 00:02:37.923
The loans manager signs the PLR change off
Four eyes: drafted by the executive, approved by the manager

00:02:37.923 --> 00:03:02.349
Sign in as Rajiv Doorgakant — Manager, Loans & Fixed Income
Loans manager — approves the PLR change campaign

00:03:02.349 --> 00:03:16.747
His notifications: the escalation from collections is already there

00:03:16.747 --> 00:03:31.899
Record who approved it — here the ALCO meeting he chaired

00:03:31.899 --> 00:03:38.661
Now move it to Approved
This time the gate lets it through

00:03:38.661 --> 00:03:43.545
Approving changes no rate by itself
The PLR, the website “Rate from” and new loan pricing change when the new rate is entered in Masters ▸ Genesis PLR History

00:03:43.545 --> 00:03:45.908
The CRM now writes a notice for every variable-rate borrower
Same balance and remaining term, new rate: the new instalment is calculated for each loan

00:03:45.908 --> 00:03:49.802
Done: the campaign moved itself to Notices generated
Notices counted on the campaign; the loans manager is told they are ready

00:03:49.802 --> 00:03:53.606
Open Loan Servicing ▸ PLR Notices

00:03:53.606 --> 00:03:57.868
PLR Notices: one per loan — borrower, new rate, change in instalment
Fixed-rate and settled loans are left out

00:03:57.868 --> 00:03:59.345
Open the notice for LMS-08821

00:03:59.345 --> 00:04:12.889
Old and new rate, old and new instalment
The loan's margin is kept: only the PLR part of the rate moves

00:04:12.889 --> 00:04:19.579
The personalised letter was generated and filed on the notice
Docs tab — ready to email, print or post

00:04:19.579 --> 00:04:28.668
Rate and instalment before and after the effective date
The term of the loan does not change

00:04:28.668 --> 00:04:36.846
Notices checked: move the campaign to Distributed
Every notice is emailed to its borrower, in English or French

00:04:36.846 --> 00:04:42.190
Distributed: the emails go out and each notice is marked Sent

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:49.602
Every notice is now Sent, with the date
The delivery log: bounces are flagged for a call or a letter by post

00:04:49.602 --> 00:04:53.367
The email is on the notice's Activity timeline
What the borrower was told, and when

00:04:53.367 --> 00:05:07.592
Dashboard ▸ Loan Book
Outstanding by product, arrears buckets, LTV bands, PLR-linked share and collections outcomes

00:05:07.592 --> 00:05:12.348
The promise to pay just logged is in the collections outcomes
Click any chart to open the accounts behind it

00:05:12.348 --> 00:05:19.829
Loan Servicing
The LMS keeps the books; the CRM services the borrowers.
